---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, SITE_TITLE, RELATIONS, pageHref } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title={`Method · ${SITE_NAME}`}>
  <header class="wrap site-head">
    <a class="site-name" href={pageHref()}>{SITE_NAME}</a>
    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
      <a href={pageHref()}>All movements and words</a>
      <a href={pageHref('about')}>About</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Method</h1>
      <h2>What counts as a movement</h2>
      <p>A movement, or ism, is mapped here when it passes three tests. It is a whole view of AI: what AI is, where it is heading and what we should do about it. It was born in the tech world, among people who build, fund or think inside the AI industry. And its own people use its name, with founding texts, a vocabulary and institutions that can be traced.</p>
      <h2>The history of AI</h2>
      <p>The history of AI is the ground all eight movements stand on: the machines, ideas, laboratories, money and laws. It runs newest first, in eras, back to the oldest documented root. Each moment is tagged with the movements it shaped and the key words it belongs to, and each era shows which movements were named in it and which words were coined.</p>
      <h2>Families, key words and the vocabulary</h2>
      <p>The eight movements are grouped in four families: transcendence, acceleration, risk and protection. Below them are the words the debate keeps returning to. Every word is in the vocabulary, with what it means and who coined it, and when. A few are key words, with a page of their own that compares how the movements see them. Criticism is not a separate section: each page ends with who disputes it.</p>
      <h2>How roots are marked</h2>
      <p>Every root in a timeline says how it is connected to the ism today. The most important difference is between ancestors the movement claims for itself and ancestors that historians attribute to it.</p>
      <ul>
        {Object.values(RELATIONS).map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Every entry names its source. Texts are first drafted, then checked claim by claim against those sources by a second reader. Entries not yet checked are marked as drafts.</p>
      <h2>Images</h2>
      <p>All images are made by people, never generated by AI. Each names its source and its rights. Images whose rights are not yet cleared are shown as labelled placeholders.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
